  'An organization uses AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager to orchestrate its incident response workflows. A critical incident has been detected, and the incident response team needs to execute a pre-defined playbook to manage the situation efficiently, ensuring all necessary steps are followed and stakeholders are informed. The goal is a coordinated and rapid response.',
  'ordering',
  '["Assign incident roles and contacts to the incident, ensuring clear responsibilities.","Review the automated actions and manual steps defined within the Incident Manager playbook to understand the workflow.","Launch the Incident Manager playbook for the detected incident to initiate the response.","Monitor the playbook''s execution and task completion in the AWS Systems Manager Incident Manager console."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'Effective incident management with Systems Manager Incident Manager starts with understanding the plan and assigning responsibilities. Option B (correct) is the initial step to familiarize the team with the playbook. Option A (correct) ensures that roles are clearly defined for the response. Option C (correct) then formally initiates the incident response process. Option D (correct) is critical for tracking progress and ensuring all steps are completed, allowing for real-time adjustments if needed.',
