  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'For an Amazon RDS compromise, the first step (Option C) is to identify the affected instance and its associated security groups. Next, (Option A) modify the security groups to restrict network access, effectively isolating the database. Then, (Option D) disable public accessibility for the RDS instance if it was enabled, further reducing its attack surface. Finally, (Option B) create a manual snapshot of the RDS instance to preserve its state for forensic analysis.',
