  'A security team is developing an incident response playbook for their AWS environment. Order the high-level phases of a typical incident response lifecycle.',
  'ordering',
  '["Detection and Analysis","Containment, Eradication, and Recovery","Post-Incident Activity","Preparation"]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'The incident response lifecycle typically begins with Preparation (Option D), which involves setting up tools, policies, and training. This is followed by Detection and Analysis (Option A) when an incident is identified and investigated. Once an incident is understood, the next phase is Containment, Eradication, and Recovery (Option B) to mitigate the impact and restore services. Finally, Post-Incident Activity (Option C) involves lessons learned, reporting, and improving future response capabilities.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain54_12',
