INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_34',
  'An organization needs to protect its high-visibility web application from sophisticated Layer 7 DDoS attacks and requires expert support during an incident. Which AWS service is recommended?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rely on AWS Shield Standard.","Subscribe to AWS Shield Advanced.","Implement AWS WAF rate-based rules only.","Use a third-party DDoS mitigation service outside AWS."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Shield Advanced, which offers enhanced DDoS protection, including protection against sophisticated Layer 7 attacks, and provides 24/7 access to the AWS DDoS Response Team for expert support during incidents. Option A (AWS Shield Standard) provides basic protection but lacks advanced features and expert support. Option C (AWS WAF rate-based rules) can help but is not a complete solution for sophisticated Layer 7 DDoS attacks, nor does it include expert support. Option D is an external solution, not an AWS service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_35',
  'A global content delivery network needs to enforce HTTPS for all viewer connections and restrict access to its Amazon S3 origins. Which CloudFront features should be used?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure CloudFront to use HTTP only and restrict S3 bucket policies.","Use AWS WAF geo-restriction and IP whitelisting.","Configure CloudFront to require HTTPS and use Origin Access Control (OAC).","Enable AWS Shield Advanced on the CloudFront distribution."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is to configure CloudFront to require HTTPS for viewer connections to ensure encryption in transit, and to use Origin Access Control (OAC) to restrict direct public access to Amazon S3 origins, ensuring content is only delivered through CloudFront. Option A is incorrect as it specifies HTTP only. Option B (AWS WAF geo-restriction and IP whitelisting) can restrict access but doesn''t enforce HTTPS or secure the origin directly. Option D (AWS Shield Advanced) provides DDoS protection, not origin access control or HTTPS enforcement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_36',
  'Which AWS service provides a web application firewall that helps protect web applications from common web exploits such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Shield Advanced","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS WAF","AWS Network Firewall"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall), which helps protect web applications or APIs against common web exploits that may affect availability, compromise security, or consume excessive resources. Option A, AWS Shield Advanced, provides DDoS protection. Option B, Amazon GuardDuty, is a threat detection service. Option D, AWS Network Firewall, provides stateful inspection for general network traffic within a VPC, not specifically for web application exploits.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_37',
  'What is the primary benefit of using AWS Shield Advanced over AWS Shield Standard for DDoS protection?',
  'mcq',
  '["Shield Standard provides automatic protection against all Layer 3/4 and Layer 7 DDoS attacks.","Shield Advanced provides enhanced detection, access to the DDoS Response Team (DRT), and cost protection for scaling.","Shield Advanced is a free service, offering basic protection for all AWS customers.","Shield Standard offers near-real-time attack visibility and custom mitigation rules."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes the primary benefits of AWS Shield Advanced. It provides enhanced detection and mitigation against more sophisticated and larger DDoS attacks, access to the 24/7 AWS DDoS Response Team (DRT), and cost protection against scaling charges resulting from a DDoS attack. Option A is incorrect; Shield Standard provides automatic protection against common Layer 3/4 attacks but not sophisticated Layer 7 attacks (anti-pattern ap-3.1-001). Option C is incorrect; Shield Advanced is a paid service. Option D is incorrect; near-real-time attack visibility and custom mitigation rules are features of Shield Advanced, not Shield Standard.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_38',
  'Which Amazon CloudFront feature ensures that end-users always connect to CloudFront using HTTPS, encrypting all communication between the viewer and CloudFront?',
  'mcq',
  '["Viewer Protocol Policy set to ''Redirect HTTP to HTTPS'' or ''HTTPS Only''.","Origin Protocol Policy set to ''HTTPS Only''.","AWS WAF integration with a custom rule for HTTPS.","Configuring a Network Access Control List (NACL) to block HTTP traffic."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) describes the CloudFront Viewer Protocol Policy, specifically setting it to ''Redirect HTTP to HTTPS'' or ''HTTPS Only'', which ensures that all communication between viewers and CloudFront is encrypted using HTTPS. Option B, the Origin Protocol Policy, controls the protocol CloudFront uses to communicate with the origin, not the viewer. Option C, while AWS WAF can enforce HTTPS, the native CloudFront viewer protocol policy is the direct and most efficient way to achieve this. Option D, configuring a NACL, is a network-level control that would block traffic but is not the specific CloudFront feature for enforcing HTTPS at the viewer level.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_39',
  'What is the purpose of a rate-based rule in AWS WAF?',
  'mcq',
  '["To block requests based on the geographic location of the client.","To count and block web requests from a single IP address that exceed a specified threshold within a five-minute period.","To inspect the content of web requests for malicious patterns like SQL injection.","To enforce HTTPS communication between the client and the web application."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes a rate-based rule in AWS WAF: it counts the number of web requests that arrive from a single IP address in a configurable five-minute period and blocks requests from IP addresses that exceed a specified threshold. Option A describes geo-restriction. Option C describes a regular rule that inspects request content. Option D describes HTTPS enforcement, typically handled by CloudFront or an Application Load Balancer.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_40',
  'A company hosts a public-facing web application behind Amazon CloudFront and needs to protect it from common web exploits such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting. Which service should be integrated with CloudFront to meet this security requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Shield Standard","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS WAF","AWS Network Firewall"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS WAF, a web application firewall specifically designed to protect web applications or APIs against common web exploits like SQL injection and cross-site scripting. It integrates seamlessly with Amazon CloudFront. Option A, AWS Shield Standard, provides basic DDoS protection at Layers 3 and 4, but not application-layer exploit protection. Option B, Amazon GuardDuty, is a threat detection service that monitors for malicious activity but does not actively block web exploits. Option D, AWS Network Firewall, provides stateful inspection within a VPC, not for edge web application protection.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_41',
  'Which AWS service allows for centralized management and deployment of AWS WAF rules, AWS Shield Advanced protections, and other network security policies across multiple AWS accounts within an AWS Organization?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations","AWS Security Hub","AWS Config","AWS Firewall Manager"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is AWS Firewall Manager, which provides centralized management and deployment of security policies, including AWS WAF rules and AWS Shield Advanced protections, across multiple accounts in an AWS Organization. Option A, AWS Organizations, is used to manage multiple AWS accounts but does not provide centralized security policy management. Option B, AWS Security Hub, aggregates security findings but does not deploy or manage policies. Option C, AWS Config, assesses and audits configurations but is not a policy deployment tool for WAF or Shield.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  66,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_42',
  'An e-commerce website experiences frequent application-layer DDoS attacks that bypass basic network protections. The security team needs advanced detection, a dedicated response team, and cost protection for scaling. Which AWS service should they utilize?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Shield Advanced","AWS Shield Standard","AWS WAF with custom rules","Amazon GuardDuty"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Shield Advanced, which provides enhanced DDoS protection against sophisticated application-layer attacks, access to the 24/7 AWS DDoS Response Team (DRT), and cost protection against scaling charges due to a DDoS event. Option B, AWS Shield Standard, provides automatic protection against common Layer 3/4 attacks but lacks the advanced features, DRT access, and cost protection needed for sophisticated application-layer attacks (anti-pattern ap-3.1-001). Option C, while AWS WAF can help mitigate some application-layer attacks, it does not provide the comprehensive DDoS protection, DRT access, or cost protection offered by Shield Advanced. Option D, Amazon GuardDuty, is a threat detection service, not a DDoS mitigation service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_43',
  'A web application needs to restrict access based on the geographic location of the user. Which AWS WAF feature can achieve this?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rate-based rules","Managed rule groups","Geo-restriction","Bot Control"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS WAF geo-restriction, which allows you to block or allow web requests based on the country or geographic location that the requests originate from. Option A, Rate-based rules, block requests based on the rate of requests from a single IP address. Option B, Managed rule groups, are pre-configured sets of rules for common threats. Option D, Bot Control, helps manage common and egregious bots.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  68,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_44',
  'A company needs to protect its public-facing web application hosted on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer from common web exploits and bots. The security team wants to block specific malicious IP addresses and prevent SQL injection attacks. Which AWS service should be used to implement these protections?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS WAF","AWS Shield Advanced","Amazon Inspector","AWS Network Firewall"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall), which helps protect web applications or APIs against common web exploits and bots that may affect availability, compromise security, or consume excessive resources. It allows creating custom rules to block specific IP addresses and includes managed rule groups to protect against common threats like SQL injection. Option B (AWS Shield Advanced) provides enhanced DDoS protection but does not offer granular web application firewall capabilities like blocking specific IP addresses or SQL injection attacks. Option C (Amazon Inspector) is a vulnerability management service for EC2 instances and container images, not a web application firewall. Option D (AWS Network Firewall) provides stateful inspection for VPC traffic, not edge protection for web applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  69,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_45',
  'A global e-commerce platform uses Amazon CloudFront to distribute its content. The security team requires that all communication between clients and CloudFront, and between CloudFront and the origin servers, must use HTTPS to ensure data in transit is encrypted. Which CloudFront security feature should be configured to meet this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Implement AWS WAF geo-restriction rules.","Configure CloudFront to enforce HTTPS for viewer and origin protocols.","Enable AWS Shield Advanced on the CloudFront distribution.","Use AWS Firewall Manager to deploy a WAF policy."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is to configure CloudFront to enforce HTTPS for both viewer protocol policy (communication between clients and CloudFront) and origin protocol policy (communication between CloudFront and origin servers). This ensures end-to-end encryption for data in transit. Option A (Implement AWS WAF geo-restriction rules) is used to block or allow traffic based on geographical location, not to enforce HTTPS. Option C (Enable AWS Shield Advanced on the CloudFront distribution) provides DDoS protection but does not enforce HTTPS. Option D (Use AWS Firewall Manager to deploy a WAF policy) can centrally manage WAF rules, but the specific configuration for HTTPS enforcement is done directly within the CloudFront distribution settings.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  70,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_46',
  'What is the primary purpose of AWS Firewall Manager in the context of AWS WAF?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provide advanced DDoS protection for web applications.","To centrally configure and manage AWS WAF rules across multiple accounts and resources.","To scan EC2 instances for vulnerabilities and compliance issues.","To enable stateful inspection of network traffic within a VPC."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) states that AWS Firewall Manager is used to centrally configure and manage AWS WAF rules across multiple accounts and resources. This simplifies the deployment and maintenance of security policies. Option A (To provide advanced DDoS protection for web applications) is the primary purpose of AWS Shield Advanced. Option C (To scan EC2 instances for vulnerabilities and compliance issues) describes the function of Amazon Inspector. Option D (To enable stateful inspection of network traffic within a VPC) describes the primary function of AWS Network Firewall.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  71,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_47',
  'A security engineer needs to restrict access to a web application served via Amazon CloudFront based on the geographic location of the client. Only users from specific countries should be allowed to access the content. Which AWS WAF feature should be configured?',
  'mcq',
  '["Rate-based rules","Bot Control managed rule group","Geo-restriction rules","Custom HTTP header inspection"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Geo-restriction rules, a feature of AWS WAF that allows you to block or allow web requests based on the country that the requests originate from. Option A (Rate-based rules) are used to automatically block IP addresses that send too many requests within a specified time period. Option B (Bot Control managed rule group) is designed to detect and block common bot traffic. Option D (Custom HTTP header inspection) can be used for various filtering based on HTTP headers but is not specifically designed for geographic restriction.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_48',
  'What is the primary purpose of CloudFront Origin Access Control (OAC)?',
  'mcq',
  '["To prevent Layer 7 DDoS attacks on CloudFront distributions.","To restrict direct access to Amazon S3 origins, ensuring content is delivered only through CloudFront.","To automatically compress content delivered from S3 origins.","To manage SSL/TLS certificates for CloudFront distributions."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) states that CloudFront Origin Access Control (OAC) is used to restrict direct access to Amazon S3 origins, ensuring that users can only access content through the CloudFront distribution. This prevents bypassing CloudFront''s security and caching features. Option A (To prevent Layer 7 DDoS attacks on CloudFront distributions) is a function of AWS WAF and AWS Shield. Option C (To automatically compress content delivered from S3 origins) is a CloudFront feature, but not the primary purpose of OAC. Option D (To manage SSL/TLS certificates for CloudFront distributions) is handled by AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) integrated with CloudFront.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_49',
  'A company wants to implement a centralized security policy for AWS WAF across multiple AWS accounts in its organization. This policy should ensure that all newly created Application Load Balancers and Amazon CloudFront distributions automatically have a specific WAF Web ACL associated with them. Which service can achieve this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations","AWS Config","AWS Firewall Manager","AWS Systems Manager"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Firewall Manager. It allows security administrators to centrally configure and manage firewall rules across multiple accounts and resources in AWS Organizations. This includes automatically applying AWS WAF Web ACLs to new and existing resources like Application Load Balancers and CloudFront distributions. Option A (AWS Organizations) is used for managing multiple AWS accounts but doesn''t provide centralized security policy deployment for services like WAF. Option B (AWS Config) helps assess, audit, and evaluate the configurations of your AWS resources, but it doesn''t deploy or manage WAF policies. Option D (AWS Systems Manager) is used for operational tasks like patching and automation, not for centralized WAF policy deployment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_1_50',
  'Which AWS service provides automatic inline protection against common Layer 3 and Layer 4 DDoS attacks without requiring any configuration?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS WAF","AWS Shield Advanced","AWS Shield Standard","AWS Network Firewall"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Shield Standard. It is automatically enabled for all AWS customers at no additional cost and provides automatic inline protection against common Layer 3 (network layer) and Layer 4 (transport layer) DDoS attacks. Option A (AWS WAF) is a web application firewall for Layer 7 attacks and requires configuration. Option B (AWS Shield Advanced) provides enhanced DDoS protection for higher-level attacks and additional features but is a paid service that requires explicit enablement. Option D (AWS Network Firewall) provides stateful inspection within a VPC and is not a DDoS protection service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_1',
  'medium'
);

