  'Which AWS service is used to centrally deploy and manage AWS WAF rules across multiple accounts and resources within an AWS Organization?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager","AWS CloudFormation","AWS Firewall Manager","AWS Organizations"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Firewall Manager. It allows security administrators to centrally configure and manage firewall rules, including AWS WAF Web ACLs, across multiple accounts and resources in AWS Organizations. Option A (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational tasks like patching and automation. Option B (AWS CloudFormation) is an infrastructure as code service for provisioning resources, but not for centralized policy management across an organization. Option D (AWS Organizations) is for managing multiple AWS accounts but doesn''t deploy or manage WAF policies itself.',
