  'To establish a secure Amazon VPC, the foundational steps must follow a logical order. Option A (correct) is the first step, as a VPC provides the isolated network environment. Option B (correct) involves creating subnets within the VPC to segment the network. Option C (correct) is then configuring route tables to control traffic flow between subnets and to the internet or other networks. Finally, Option D (correct) involves creating security groups to act as virtual firewalls at the instance level, controlling inbound and outbound traffic for EC2 instances.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
