INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_2_81',
  'A security engineer needs to configure a new security group for an Amazon EC2 instance to allow inbound SSH access only from a specific IP address range and outbound HTTP/HTTPS access to the internet. Order the steps to correctly configure this security group.',
  'ordering',
  '["Add an inbound rule for SSH (TCP port 22) allowing traffic from the specified IP address range.","Create a new security group in the Amazon VPC.","Add an outbound rule for HTTP (TCP port 80) and HTTPS (TCP port 443) allowing traffic to 0.0.0.0/0.","Associate the security group with the Amazon EC2 instance."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To correctly configure a security group, you must first create it. Option B (correct) is the initial step. Next, you define the inbound rules, such as allowing SSH from a specific IP range, as in Option A. After inbound rules, you define outbound rules, like allowing HTTP/HTTPS to the internet, as in Option C. Finally, the security group must be associated with the EC2 instance for the rules to take effect, as in Option D. Incorrect orders would either attempt to add rules or associate the group before its creation, or apply rules before defining them.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_2_82',
  'A company wants to deploy AWS Network Firewall within their Amazon VPC to provide stateful inspection for traffic between their public and private subnets. Order the steps required to set up AWS Network Firewall.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a firewall policy and define rule groups (stateful and stateless).","Create an AWS Network Firewall endpoint in each availability zone where traffic needs to be inspected.","Update the route tables for the subnets to route traffic through the firewall endpoints.","Create an AWS Network Firewall resource and associate it with the firewall policy."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'The first step in deploying AWS Network Firewall is to define the security logic by creating a firewall policy and associated rule groups, as in Option A. Once the policy is defined, you create the AWS Network Firewall resource itself and link it to the policy, as in Option D. After the firewall is created, you must create firewall endpoints in the relevant Availability Zones to inspect traffic, as in Option B. Finally, to direct traffic through these endpoints, you update the route tables of the subnets, as in Option C. Incorrect orders would attempt to create the firewall or endpoints before defining the policy, or route traffic before the firewall infrastructure is in place.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_2_83',
  'A development team needs to securely access Amazon S3 buckets from EC2 instances in a private subnet without traversing the internet. Order the steps to establish a secure VPC endpoint for Amazon S3.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 (Gateway type).","Add an endpoint policy to restrict S3 access to specific buckets or IAM roles.","Update the route tables of the private subnets to include a route to the S3 endpoint.","Verify connectivity from an EC2 instance in the private subnet to Amazon S3."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To establish a secure VPC endpoint for Amazon S3, the first step is to create the VPC endpoint itself, which for S3 is a Gateway type endpoint, as in Option A. Once the endpoint is created, you must update the route tables of the private subnets to direct traffic destined for S3 through this endpoint, as in Option C. After routing is configured, you can apply an endpoint policy to further restrict access to S3, enhancing security, as in Option B. Finally, it is crucial to verify that the EC2 instances can successfully connect to S3 through the endpoint, as in Option D. Incorrect orders might attempt to apply policies or verify connectivity before the endpoint or routing is established.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_2_84',
  'A company wants to centrally manage AWS WAF web ACLs across multiple accounts and regions using AWS Firewall Manager. Order the steps to achieve this centralized management.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure AWS Firewall Manager in the AWS Organizations management account.","Create an AWS WAF web ACL and associate it with a Firewall Manager policy.","Apply the Firewall Manager policy to target accounts or organizational units (OUs).","Ensure AWS Config is enabled in all member accounts."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'To centrally manage AWS WAF with AWS Firewall Manager, the initial step is to set up Firewall Manager in the AWS Organizations management account, as in Option A. AWS Firewall Manager relies on AWS Config to evaluate compliance, so ensuring AWS Config is enabled in all member accounts is a prerequisite, as in Option D. Next, you create the AWS WAF web ACL that defines your security rules and associate it with a Firewall Manager policy, as in Option B. Finally, you apply this Firewall Manager policy to the desired target accounts or OUs within your organization, as in Option C, to enforce the WAF rules centrally. Incorrect orders would attempt to create policies or apply them before the foundational setup of Firewall Manager and AWS Config.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_56_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_56_m_56_2_85',
  'A system administrator needs to configure an existing security group to allow inbound HTTPS traffic from anywhere for a web server. Order the steps to modify the security group.',
  'ordering',
  '["Navigate to the EC2 console and select ''Security Groups''.","Select the target security group.","Add an inbound rule: Type ''HTTPS'', Protocol ''TCP'', Port Range ''443'', Source ''0.0.0.0/0''.","Save the inbound rules."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To modify an existing security group, the first step is to navigate to the EC2 console and specifically select ''Security Groups'', as in Option A. Next, you must identify and select the specific security group that needs modification, as in Option B. Once the correct security group is selected, you can proceed to add the desired inbound rule, specifying HTTPS, TCP port 443, and the source as 0.0.0.0/0 for anywhere, as in Option C. Finally, you must save the changes for the new rule to take effect, as in Option D. Incorrect orders would attempt to add rules before selecting the security group or navigate away before saving changes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain56_12',
  NOW(),
  9,
