  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'Enabling AWS Shield Advanced protection for an Amazon Route 53 hosted zone requires a specific order of actions. Option D (correct) is the prerequisite, as you must first subscribe to the AWS Shield Advanced service. Option A (correct) then involves selecting the specific Route 53 hosted zone resource that you want to protect. Option B (correct) is to configure your DDoS response team contacts, ensuring that the Shield Response Team (SRT) can reach the appropriate personnel during an attack. Finally, Option C (correct) is to review the protection status to confirm that Shield Advanced is actively monitoring and protecting your resource.',
