  'To monitor for privilege escalation attempts, the first step is to configure AWS CloudTrail to send management events to a CloudWatch Logs log group (Option B), as these events contain API call information. Next, create a CloudWatch metric filter within that log group to extract specific API call events that indicate potential privilege escalation (Option A). After the metric filter is set, create a CloudWatch alarm that triggers when the count generated by the metric filter exceeds a defined threshold (Option C). Finally, it is crucial to test the alarm by performing the monitored API call and verifying that the alert is generated as expected (Option D).',
