  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To configure security alerting on VPC Flow Logs, the initial step is to enable VPC Flow Logs to send network traffic data to Amazon CloudWatch Logs (Option A). Once logs are flowing, create an Amazon CloudWatch metric filter within the log group to specifically identify and count denied traffic originating from the suspicious IP address (Option B). Following this, create an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm that monitors the metric generated by the filter and triggers when the count of denied traffic exceeds a predefined threshold (Option C). Finally, configure an Amazon SNS topic to receive notifications from the CloudWatch Alarm, ensuring the security team is alerted in real-time (Option D).',
