  'A compliance team needs to be notified and log all non-compliant resource changes detected by AWS Config. Order the steps to set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture AWS Config compliance changes for security auditing.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern matching AWS Config compliance change events.","Enable AWS Config to record resource configurations and evaluate compliance.","Configure an Amazon SQS queue or AWS Lambda function as the target for the EventBridge rule.","Verify that compliance change events are being captured and processed by the target."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To capture AWS Config compliance changes for security auditing, the first step is to enable AWS Config to record resource configurations and evaluate compliance against defined rules (Option B). Once Config is active, create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern specifically designed to match AWS Config compliance change events (Option A). Following this, configure an Amazon SQS queue for reliable delivery or an AWS Lambda function for immediate processing as the target for the EventBridge rule (Option C). Finally, verify that compliance change events are being successfully captured by EventBridge and processed by the chosen target to ensure the auditing solution is functional (Option D).',
