  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'When investigating missing CloudTrail events from an EC2 instance, the initial step is to confirm that the API calls in question are management events and not data events (Option D), as this dictates the logging configuration. Next, verify that the CloudTrail trail is enabled and configured to log management events (Option A). Then, check the IAM role attached to the EC2 instance for necessary permissions to make the API calls (Option B), as unauthorized calls won''t generate successful events. Finally, review the CloudTrail event history for any events originating from the EC2 instance''s principal (Option C) to see what, if anything, is being logged.',
