  'Application logs from an Amazon EC2 instance are not appearing in Amazon CloudWatch Logs, despite the CloudWatch agent being installed. Order the steps to troubleshoot this issue.',
  'ordering',
  '["Verify the IAM role attached to the EC2 instance has permissions to write to CloudWatch Logs.","Check the status of the CloudWatch Logs agent on the EC2 instance.","Review the CloudWatch Logs agent configuration file for correct log paths and log group names.","Examine the EC2 instance''s network connectivity to CloudWatch Logs endpoints."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To troubleshoot missing application logs from an EC2 instance in CloudWatch Logs, the initial step is to check the status of the CloudWatch Logs agent on the EC2 instance to ensure it is running (Option B). Next, review the CloudWatch Logs agent configuration file to confirm that the log paths are correct and the specified CloudWatch Log Group names are accurate (Option C). Following this, verify the IAM role attached to the EC2 instance, ensuring it has the necessary permissions to write log events to CloudWatch Logs (Option A). Finally, examine the EC2 instance''s network connectivity to CloudWatch Logs endpoints, especially if it''s in a private subnet, to rule out network issues (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain55_12',
  NOW(),
