  '{"A":"Centralized firewall rules","B":"Private access to S3","C":"Granular instance traffic control"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'For centralized firewall rules within a VPC, AWS Network Firewall (Option A) provides stateful inspection. To enable private access to Amazon S3 from within a VPC without traversing the internet, a VPC Endpoint for S3 (Option B) is the appropriate solution. Granular traffic control for individual EC2 instances is achieved using Security Groups (Option C).',
