  '{"A":"Check security groups","B":"Check Network ACLs","C":"Review route tables"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'When troubleshooting, checking security groups focuses on instance-level inbound and outbound rules that might be blocking traffic. Checking Network ACLs involves reviewing subnet-level inbound and outbound rules, which are stateless and can block traffic in both directions. Reviewing route tables is crucial to understand how traffic is directed within your VPC and between connected networks.',
