  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon API Gateway) is commonly used to enforce HTTPS for APIs. It integrates with AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to associate SSL/TLS certificates with custom domains, ensuring secure communication for API endpoints. Option A (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service. Option B (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database. Option D (Amazon SQS) is a message queuing service.',
