INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_58_m_58_3_28',
  'Which AWS service enables the automatic rotation of database credentials, API keys, and other secrets, improving security posture and reducing operational overhead?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)","AWS Secrets Manager","Amazon S3","AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Secrets Manager) is the correct service that enables automatic rotation of database credentials, API keys, and other secrets. This helps improve security by regularly changing credentials without manual intervention. Option A (AWS KMS) manages encryption keys. Option C (Amazon S3) is object storage. Option D (AWS IAM) manages access permissions to AWS resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain58_12',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_58_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_58_m_58_3_29',
  'What Amazon S3 feature allows you to define rules for automatically moving objects between different storage classes or deleting them after a specified period?',
  'mcq',
  '["S3 Versioning","S3 Object Lock","S3 Lifecycle Policies","S3 Block Public Access"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (S3 Lifecycle Policies) is the Amazon S3 feature that allows you to define rules for automating the management of objects throughout their lifecycle, including transitioning them to different storage classes or expiring/deleting them after a specified time. Option A (S3 Versioning) keeps multiple versions of an object. Option B (S3 Object Lock) provides WORM capabilities. Option D (S3 Block Public Access) prevents public access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain58_12',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_58_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_58_m_58_3_30',
  'Which Amazon S3 feature is designed to help meet regulatory requirements by preventing objects from being deleted or overwritten for a fixed amount of time or indefinitely?',
  'mcq',
  '["S3 Versioning","S3 Object Lock","S3 Intelligent-Tiering","S3 Replication"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (S3 Object Lock) is the Amazon S3 feature specifically designed to help meet regulatory requirements by enforcing a write-once-read-many (WORM) model. This prevents objects from being deleted or overwritten for a specified retention period. Option A (S3 Versioning) keeps multiple versions of an object. Option C (S3 Intelligent-Tiering) optimizes storage costs by moving objects between access tiers. Option D (S3 Replication) copies objects between buckets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain58_12',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_58_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_58_m_58_3_31',
  'To control where data is physically stored in Amazon S3 for data residency compliance, which feature allows you to specify the geographic location of your buckets?',
  'mcq',
  '["S3 Object Ownership","S3 Bucket Policies","S3 Bucket Location Constraints","S3 Access Points"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (S3 Bucket Location Constraints) is the feature that allows you to specify the geographic AWS Region where your Amazon S3 bucket and its objects will be stored, which is crucial for data residency compliance. Option A (S3 Object Ownership) controls who owns objects in a bucket. Option B (S3 Bucket Policies) define access permissions. Option D (S3 Access Points) simplify data access for applications.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain58_12',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_58_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_58_m_58_3_32',
  'What action can be taken on an AWS KMS key to temporarily prevent its use for cryptographic operations without deleting it?',
  'mcq',
  '["Delete the key immediately.","Disable the KMS key.","Revoke all grants on the key.","Change the key policy to deny all users."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Disable the KMS key) is the correct action to temporarily prevent a KMS key from being used for cryptographic operations. A disabled key can be re-enabled later. Option A (Delete the key immediately) is irreversible and not temporary. Option C (Revoke all grants) and Option D (Change the key policy) are access control mechanisms, but disabling is a direct operational state change for the key itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain58_12',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_58_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_58_m_58_3_33',
  'A security team is decommissioning an application that used an AWS KMS key for encryption. To prevent accidental data loss, what is the most secure approach for deleting the KMS key?',
  'mcq',
  '["Immediately delete the KMS key to minimize exposure.","Disable the KMS key, then delete it after a 7-day waiting period.","Schedule the KMS key for deletion with the mandatory waiting period.","Revoke all IAM permissions for the KMS key and then delete it."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Schedule the KMS key for deletion with the mandatory waiting period) is the most secure approach. AWS KMS enforces a 7-30 day waiting period, which is crucial to ensure no data is inadvertently made inaccessible (anti-pattern ap-5.3-001). Option A (immediately delete) is dangerous. Option B (disable then delete after 7 days) is close, but ''scheduling for deletion'' automatically applies the mandatory waiting period, which is the standard and safest process. Option D (revoke permissions then delete) doesn''t guarantee the safety net of the waiting period.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain58_12',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
