  '["Amazon S3","AWS Secrets Manager","AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store","Amazon DynamoDB"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Secrets Manager) is best suited for securely storing and retrieving API keys, offering encryption, fine-grained access control, and optional automatic rotation. Option A (Amazon S3) is object storage, not ideal for managing secrets. Option C (AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store) can store secrets but lacks the advanced features like automatic rotation found in Secrets Manager. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database, not a dedicated secret management service.',
