  '{3}',
  'Option D (AWS Secrets Manager) is the correct service. AWS Secrets Manager helps you protect access to your applications, services, and IT resources by enabling you to easily rotate, manage, and retrieve database credentials, API keys, and other secrets throughout their lifecycle. Option A (AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS)) is for managing encryption keys, not application secrets. Option B (AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)) manages user and service access to AWS resources. Option C (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service.',
