INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_29',
  'Which AWS service helps organizations establish a secure, multi-account AWS environment with a well-architected landing zone and ongoing governance?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Control Tower","AWS Organizations","Amazon Security Hub","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Control Tower, which provides a simplified way to set up and govern a secure, multi-account AWS environment, known as a landing zone. It automates the setup of core accounts, implements guardrails, and centralizes logging and security. Option B (AWS Organizations) is used by Control Tower to manage accounts, but Control Tower itself provides the landing zone and governance. Option C (Amazon Security Hub) aggregates security findings but does not establish the multi-account structure. Option D (AWS Config) assesses and audits resource configurations but does not set up the initial landing zone.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_30',
  'An organization wants to centrally manage multiple AWS accounts and apply common policies across them. Which AWS service is foundational for creating a multi-account structure with Organizational Units (OUs)?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Service Catalog","AWS Organizations","AWS CloudFormation","AWS Audit Manager"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is AWS Organizations, which allows you to consolidate multiple AWS accounts into an organization that you create and centrally manage. It enables you to create Organizational Units (OUs) to group accounts and apply policies. Option A (AWS Service Catalog) helps users provision approved IT services. Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is for provisioning infrastructure as code. Option D (AWS Audit Manager) helps automate evidence collection for audits. While these services can operate within an Organizations structure, AWS Organizations itself provides the multi-account management and OU hierarchy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_31',
  'What is the primary purpose of Service Control Policies (SCPs) within AWS Organizations?',
  'mcq',
  '["To grant permissions to IAM users and roles within an account.","To define resource tagging standards across accounts.","To set maximum permissions for accounts, OUs, or the entire organization.","To detect non-compliant resource configurations."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) describes the primary purpose of Service Control Policies (SCPs). SCPs are a type of organization policy that you can use to manage permissions in your organization. They offer central control over the maximum available permissions for all accounts in your organization, or for specific Organizational Units (OUs). Option A describes IAM policies, which grant permissions. Option B relates to resource management and governance, not directly SCPs. Option D describes the function of AWS Config rules.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_32',
  'Which AWS service allows you to deploy a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions as a single entity to ensure multi-account compliance?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Security Hub","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Organizations","AWS Config conformance packs"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is AWS Config conformance packs. These allow you to package a set of AWS Config rules and remediation actions into a single entity, which can then be deployed across multiple accounts and regions to enforce compliance. Option A (Amazon Security Hub) aggregates security findings. Option B (AWS Service Catalog) allows users to provision approved IT services. Option C (AWS Organizations) manages accounts but doesn''t deploy compliance rules directly.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_33',
  'A security team needs a centralized view of security findings from various AWS services across multiple accounts and AWS Regions. Which service can aggregate these findings for consolidated visibility?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Security Hub","AWS Audit Manager","AWS Config","AWS CloudFormation"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is Amazon Security Hub. It provides a comprehensive view of your security posture across your AWS accounts and helps you check your environment against security industry standards and best practices. It can aggregate security findings from various AWS services (like GuardDuty, Inspector, Macie) and partner solutions across multiple accounts and Regions. Option B (AWS Audit Manager) collects evidence for audits. Option C (AWS Config) evaluates resource configurations. Option D (AWS CloudFormation) provisions infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_34',
  'A company wants to establish a new multi-account AWS environment with predefined security baselines, centralized logging, and continuous governance, while minimizing manual setup. Which service should they use?',
  'mcq',
  '["Manually create accounts and configure IAM policies in each.","Deploy AWS Control Tower to set up a landing zone.","Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy security configurations.","Implement AWS Organizations to group accounts and apply SCPs."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is to deploy AWS Control Tower. Control Tower automates the setup of a secure, multi-account AWS environment (landing zone) with predefined security baselines, centralized logging, and continuous governance through guardrails, significantly minimizing manual setup. Option A (Manually create accounts and configure IAM policies) is highly operational and error-prone, violating the ''minimizing manual setup'' constraint. Option C (Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets) can deploy configurations but doesn''t establish the entire landing zone or provide ongoing governance like Control Tower. Option D (Implement AWS Organizations) is foundational for multi-account, but Control Tower builds upon Organizations to provide the full landing zone and governance features with less effort.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_35',
  'What is the primary benefit of using AWS Organizations for managing multiple AWS accounts?',
  'mcq',
  '["To automate code deployments across accounts.","To centrally monitor application performance.","To consolidate billing and apply policies across accounts.","To provide a managed relational database service."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the primary benefit of AWS Organizations. It allows you to consolidate billing for all your AWS accounts into a single payment method and apply policies, such as Service Control Policies (SCPs), across multiple accounts. Option A (To automate code deployments) is typically handled by services like AWS CodePipeline. Option B (To centrally monitor application performance) is done using services like Amazon CloudWatch. Option D (To provide a managed relational database service) describes Amazon RDS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_36',
  'Which feature of AWS Organizations allows for the programmatic creation of new AWS accounts with predefined settings?',
  'mcq',
  '["Service Control Policies (SCPs)","Organizational Units (OUs)","Account vending machine","AWS Config conformance packs"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) refers to the ''account vending machine'' concept, which is often implemented using AWS Organizations APIs (like CreateAccount) or services like AWS Control Tower, to programmatically create new accounts with standardized configurations. Option A (SCPs) define maximum permissions. Option B (OUs) group accounts. Option D (AWS Config conformance packs) assess compliance, not create accounts.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_37',
  'In AWS Control Tower, what are ''guardrails'' primarily designed to do?',
  'mcq',
  '["Enforce policies and best practices across your AWS accounts.","Monitor application logs for security threats.","Automate the deployment of infrastructure resources.","Provide a catalog of approved IT services for end-users."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is the primary function of guardrails in AWS Control Tower. Guardrails are high-level rules that provide ongoing governance for your AWS environment, helping to enforce policies and best practices. They can be preventive (using SCPs) or detective (using AWS Config rules). Option B (Monitor application logs) is done by services like Amazon CloudWatch Logs and Amazon GuardDuty. Option C (Automate infrastructure deployment) is done by AWS CloudFormation. Option D (Provide a catalog of approved IT services) is the function of AWS Service Catalog.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  9,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_38',
  'What is a key difference between an AWS Organizations Service Control Policy (SCP) and an IAM permissions policy?',
  'mcq',
  '["SCPs grant permissions, while IAM policies deny permissions.","SCPs apply to the entire organization or OUs, while IAM policies apply to individual IAM identities.","SCPs are used for resource tagging, while IAM policies control access to resources.","SCPs are detective controls, while IAM policies are preventive controls."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) highlights a key difference. SCPs apply to accounts, OUs, or the entire organization, setting maximum permissions for all IAM users and roles within those entities. IAM policies, on the other hand, are attached to individual IAM users, groups, or roles and grant or deny specific permissions. Option A is incorrect; both can deny, but SCPs set boundaries. Option C is incorrect; SCPs are not for tagging. Option D is incorrect; SCPs are preventive, and IAM policies are also preventive.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  10,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_39',
  'A security team needs to enforce a consistent set of compliance rules across all development and production accounts in their organization. Which AWS service and feature should they use for automated, multi-account compliance checks?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy individual AWS Config rules.","AWS Organizations to apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) for compliance.","Amazon Security Hub to aggregate compliance findings from various services.","AWS Config conformance packs deployed via AWS Organizations."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is the most effective solution. AWS Config conformance packs allow you to deploy a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions as a single unit across multiple accounts, often managed through AWS Organizations, ensuring consistent and automated compliance checks. Option A (CloudFormation StackSets) can deploy individual Config rules, but conformance packs are designed to bundle and manage these rules more efficiently for compliance. Option B (SCPs) are preventive controls that set permission boundaries, not for assessing configurations against compliance rules. Option C (Security Hub) aggregates findings but doesn''t perform the compliance checks itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_40',
  'What is the primary function of Amazon Security Hub?',
  'mcq',
  '["To provision new AWS resources securely.","To provide a centralized view of security alerts and compliance status.","To manage user access and permissions.","To encrypt data at rest and in transit."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the primary function of Amazon Security Hub. It aggregates, organizes, and prioritizes security alerts (findings) from various AWS services (like GuardDuty, Inspector, Macie) and AWS Partner Network (APN) solutions. It also helps you monitor your compliance with security industry standards. Option A (To provision new AWS resources securely) is typically done with services like AWS CloudFormation or AWS Service Catalog. Option C (To manage user access and permissions) is handled by AWS IAM. Option D (To encrypt data) is handled by services like AWS KMS and service-specific encryption features.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_41',
  'What is a ''landing zone'' in the context of AWS Control Tower?',
  'mcq',
  '["A well-architected, multi-account AWS environment with security and governance best practices.","A specific AWS Region where all applications are deployed.","A network segment for public-facing web servers.","A repository for storing application code and binaries."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) defines a landing zone. In AWS Control Tower, a landing zone is a well-architected, multi-account AWS environment that is a secure, scalable, and pre-configured foundation for your workloads. It incorporates security and governance best practices. Options B, C, and D describe other AWS concepts or components, not a landing zone.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_42',
  'What is the primary purpose of creating Organizational Units (OUs) within AWS Organizations?',
  'mcq',
  '["To isolate network traffic between accounts.","To group accounts for easier management and policy application.","To deploy applications across multiple AWS Regions.","To monitor resource utilization and costs."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the primary purpose of OUs. Organizational Units (OUs) allow you to group accounts into logical units, making it easier to manage them and apply Service Control Policies (SCPs) to a subset of accounts. Option A (Isolate network traffic) is done using VPCs and network configurations. Option C (Deploy applications across Regions) is a deployment strategy, not an OU function. Option D (Monitor resource utilization and costs) is done by services like Amazon CloudWatch and AWS Cost Explorer.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_43',
  'How do Service Control Policies (SCPs) primarily affect permissions in an AWS Organization?',
  'mcq',
  '["They grant specific permissions to IAM users and roles.","They define the minimum permissions required for an account.","They set the maximum available permissions for accounts, OUs, or the entire organization.","They detect when an account''s permissions are too broad."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) describes how SCPs affect permissions. SCPs act as guardrails, defining the maximum permissions that any IAM user or role within an affected account can have. They do not grant permissions; rather, they filter the permissions that IAM policies can grant. Option A is incorrect; IAM policies grant permissions. Option B is incorrect; SCPs set maximums, not minimums. Option D is a detective function, typically performed by services like IAM Access Analyzer or Security Hub.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_44',
  'An organization needs to ensure that all newly created S3 buckets across their multi-account environment have encryption enabled. Which AWS Config feature can help enforce this compliance requirement consistently?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Config rules for individual accounts.","AWS CloudFormation templates with S3 bucket policies.","AWS Organizations Service Control Policies (SCPs).","AWS Config conformance packs deployed organization-wide."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is AWS Config conformance packs deployed organization-wide. Conformance packs allow you to deploy a collection of AWS Config rules (like one checking for S3 bucket encryption) and remediation actions across multiple accounts in your organization, ensuring consistent enforcement of compliance requirements. Option A (Individual Config rules) would require manual deployment per account. Option B (CloudFormation templates) can create compliant buckets, but conformance packs *enforce* ongoing compliance. Option C (SCPs) can prevent certain actions but are not designed for detailed resource configuration assessment and enforcement like Config rules.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_1_45',
