  'Option C (To provide a centralized view of security posture across all Regions) is the primary benefit of aggregating Security Hub findings. This allows security teams to monitor and manage security across their global AWS footprint from a single console. Option A (To reduce the cost of Security Hub usage) is not a direct benefit of aggregation. Option B (To simplify the deployment of security controls) is not directly related to findings aggregation. Option D (To automate the remediation of security vulnerabilities) is a separate capability, often achieved through integration with other services.',
