INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_30',
  'Which AWS service enables organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS, ensuring compliance and governance?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Organizations","Amazon Security Hub","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Audit Manager"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Service Catalog. This service allows organizations to create, manage, and distribute catalogs of approved IT services, such as virtual machine images, servers, software, and databases. It helps achieve consistent governance and compliance by ensuring users only provision approved resources. Option A (AWS Organizations) manages accounts. Option B (Amazon Security Hub) aggregates security findings. Option D (AWS Audit Manager) collects audit evidence.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_31',
  'An organization needs to automate the collection of evidence for audit purposes across its AWS accounts to simplify compliance reporting. Which AWS service is designed for this task?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Config","Amazon Security Hub","AWS Control Tower","AWS Audit Manager"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is AWS Audit Manager. It helps you continuously audit your AWS usage to simplify how you assess risk and compliance with regulations and industry standards. It automates the collection of evidence from your AWS accounts and services. Option A (AWS Config) assesses resource configurations. Option B (Amazon Security Hub) aggregates security findings. Option C (AWS Control Tower) sets up and governs multi-account environments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_32',
  'Which type of security control aims to prevent non-compliant actions from occurring in the first place, rather than detecting them after they have happened?',
  'mcq',
  '["Preventive control","Detective control","Corrective control","Compensating control"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is a preventive control. Preventive controls are designed to stop unauthorized or non-compliant actions before they occur. Examples include Service Control Policies (SCPs), IAM permission boundaries, and resource policies. Option B (Detective control) identifies issues after they have occurred. Option C (Corrective control) fixes issues after they have been detected. Option D (Compensating control) mitigates the risk when a primary control cannot be fully met.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_33',
  'Which type of security control is Amazon GuardDuty, which identifies unusual and potentially unauthorized activity in your AWS environment?',
  'mcq',
  '["Preventive control","Corrective control","Detective control","Compensating control"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is a detective control. Detective controls monitor and identify security events or policy violations after they have occurred. Amazon GuardDuty is a prime example, as it continuously monitors for malicious activity and unauthorized behavior. Option A (Preventive control) stops actions before they occur. Option B (Corrective control) fixes issues after detection. Option D (Compensating control) provides an alternative when a primary control is not feasible.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_34',
  'What is a key benefit of using AWS CloudFormation StackSets for deploying resources?',
  'mcq',
  '["It allows users to self-provision approved IT services.","It enables deploying a CloudFormation stack to multiple accounts and Regions with a single operation.","It provides automated evidence collection for audits.","It centrally manages security findings from various services."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is a key benefit of AWS CloudFormation StackSets. StackSets allow you to create, update, or delete stacks across multiple accounts and AWS Regions from a single CloudFormation template. This is highly beneficial for consistent resource deployment in multi-account environments. Option A (Self-provisioning IT services) is a function of AWS Service Catalog. Option C (Automated evidence collection) is provided by AWS Audit Manager. Option D (Centrally managing security findings) is a function of Amazon Security Hub.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_35',
  'Which statement best describes the purpose of AWS Service Catalog?',
  'mcq',
  '["It aggregates security findings from multiple AWS services.","It provides a centralized dashboard for monitoring resource configurations.","It allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services approved for use on AWS.","It automates the collection of audit evidence from AWS accounts."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately describes AWS Service Catalog. It helps organizations manage their IT services by creating a catalog of approved products (e.g., EC2 instances, databases, software stacks) that users can then provision. This ensures compliance and consistency. Option A (Aggregating security findings) is done by Amazon Security Hub. Option B (Monitoring resource configurations) is done by AWS Config. Option D (Automating audit evidence collection) is done by AWS Audit Manager.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_36',
  'What is the primary purpose of AWS CloudFormation drift detection?',
  'mcq',
  '["To automatically update CloudFormation stacks to the latest template version.","To identify when a stack''s actual resource configuration differs from its CloudFormation template.","To prevent unauthorized users from modifying CloudFormation templates.","To deploy CloudFormation stacks across multiple AWS accounts simultaneously."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the primary purpose of CloudFormation drift detection. It allows you to identify when the actual configuration of resources in a stack has changed from the configuration specified in the CloudFormation template, indicating ''drift.'' This helps maintain configuration consistency. Option A (Automatic updates) is not what drift detection does. Option C (Preventing unauthorized modifications) is handled by IAM policies. Option D (Deploying across multiple accounts) is a function of CloudFormation StackSets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_37',
  'How does AWS Service Catalog benefit end-users in an organization?',
  'mcq',
  '["It allows them to create new AWS accounts without approval.","It provides a self-service portal to provision approved IT resources securely.","It gives them full administrative access to all AWS services.","It automatically remediates non-compliant resources."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) describes how AWS Service Catalog benefits end-users. It provides a self-service portal where users can browse and provision IT services that have been pre-approved by the organization, ensuring they deploy compliant and secure resources without needing direct AWS console access or deep AWS knowledge. Option A (Creating accounts without approval) is a security risk and not a feature. Option C (Full administrative access) violates the principle of least privilege. Option D (Automatic remediation) is a function of AWS Config with remediation actions, not Service Catalog.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_38',
  'Which type of security control is implemented to fix or restore a system to a secure state after a security incident has been detected?',
  'mcq',
  '["Corrective control","Preventive control","Detective control","Deterrent control"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is a corrective control. Corrective controls are actions taken to repair damage, restore systems, and prevent future occurrences after a security incident or non-compliance has been detected. Option B (Preventive control) aims to stop issues before they happen. Option C (Detective control) identifies issues after they occur. Option D (Deterrent control) discourages potential attackers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_39',
  'A security team needs to ensure that no IAM users can create access keys for the AWS account root user. Which type of control should be implemented to proactively block this action?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Security Hub finding","AWS Organizations Service Control Policy (SCP)","AWS Config rule with remediation","AWS Audit Manager assessment"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is an AWS Organizations Service Control Policy (SCP). SCPs are preventive controls that can be used to explicitly deny actions across an entire organization or specific OUs/accounts, such as preventing the creation of access keys for the root user. This proactively blocks the action. Option A (Security Hub finding) is a detective control, identifying the issue after it occurs. Option C (AWS Config rule with remediation) is also detective (identifies non-compliance) and then corrective (remediates), but it doesn''t prevent the initial action. Option D (Audit Manager assessment) collects evidence, which is a detective function.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_40',
  'What is the main advantage of using AWS CloudFormation StackSets over individual CloudFormation stacks?',
  'mcq',
  '["StackSets allow for manual updates to resources without templates.","StackSets enable consistent resource deployment across multiple AWS accounts and Regions from a single template.","StackSets provide a graphical interface for designing infrastructure.","StackSets automatically detect and fix configuration drift."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the main advantage. AWS CloudFormation StackSets allow you to provision, update, or delete stacks across multiple AWS accounts and Regions from a single CloudFormation template, ensuring consistency and reducing operational overhead. Option A (Manual updates) is not a feature and contradicts infrastructure as code principles. Option C (Graphical interface) is provided by AWS CloudFormation Designer, not StackSets specifically. Option D (Drift detection) is a feature of CloudFormation, but StackSets don''t automatically fix drift; they enable consistent deployment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_2_41',
  'Which AWS service is designed to help you prepare for audits by continuously collecting evidence from your AWS accounts?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Config","Amazon Security Hub","AWS Control Tower","AWS Audit Manager"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is AWS Audit Manager. This service automates the continuous collection of evidence from your AWS accounts to help you prepare for audits. It maps your AWS usage to control requirements of common industry standards and regulations. Option A (AWS Config) assesses resource configurations. Option B (Amazon Security Hub) aggregates security findings. Option C (AWS Control Tower) establishes a multi-account landing zone with governance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
