  '{1}',
  'Option B (AWS Service Catalog) allows organizations to create and manage catalogs of IT services that are approved for use on AWS. This enables users to quickly deploy only the approved versions of services, ensuring compliance with organizational standards. Option A (AWS CloudFormation) is used to provision infrastructure as code but doesn''t inherently provide a curated catalog for end-users. Option C (AWS Organizations) manages accounts and policies but not resource provisioning. Option D (AWS Config) assesses compliance of existing resources, not for provisioning approved ones.',
