INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_4_28',
  'Which AWS service provides a comprehensive view of your security posture across multiple AWS accounts and Regions by aggregating security findings from various AWS services and partner solutions?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Config","AWS Organizations","Amazon Security Hub","AWS Audit Manager"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Security Hub) is the correct choice. Amazon Security Hub is designed to give you a comprehensive view of your high-priority security alerts and compliance status across your AWS accounts. It aggregates, organizes, and prioritizes security findings from various AWS services (like GuardDuty, Inspector, Config) and partner products. Option A (AWS Config) assesses and audits resource configurations. Option B (AWS Organizations) helps you centrally manage multiple AWS accounts. Option D (AWS Audit Manager) automates evidence collection for audits. While all these services contribute to security governance, Security Hub specifically provides the aggregated security posture view.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  106,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_4_29',
  'During a security review, an architect identifies a need to ensure that all AWS accounts consistently adhere to a baseline set of security configurations, such as specific IAM password policies and S3 bucket encryption settings. Which AWS service can enforce this standard across an AWS Organization?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Service Catalog","AWS CloudFormation StackSets","AWS Config conformance packs","Amazon Security Hub"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Config conformance packs) is the correct choice. Conformance packs allow you to deploy a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions across multiple accounts in an AWS Organization. This ensures that a baseline set of security configurations, like IAM password policies or S3 encryption, is consistently applied and monitored. Option A (AWS Service Catalog) helps provision approved resources but doesn''t enforce ongoing configuration compliance. Option B (AWS CloudFormation StackSets) deploys infrastructure as code but doesn''t continuously enforce configuration compliance post-deployment. Option D (Amazon Security Hub) aggregates findings but doesn''t enforce the configurations itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  107,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_4_30',
  'What is the primary purpose of an AWS Organizations Service Control Policy (SCP) in the context of identifying and preventing security gaps?',
  'mcq',
  '["To detect non-compliant resource configurations after they occur.","To automate the collection of audit evidence for compliance reports.","To define the maximum available permissions for accounts within an Organization.","To aggregate security findings from multiple AWS services into a central dashboard."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (To define the maximum available permissions for accounts within an Organization) is the correct answer. SCPs are a type of preventive control that sets permission guardrails for all accounts in an Organizational Unit (OU) or the entire organization. By limiting what actions accounts can take, SCPs effectively prevent certain security gaps from ever occurring. Option A (To detect non-compliant resource configurations) describes AWS Config. Option B (To automate the collection of audit evidence) describes AWS Audit Manager. Option D (To aggregate security findings) describes Amazon Security Hub.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  108,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_4',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_59_m_59_4_31',
  'A security team is conducting an architectural review and wants to identify if any AWS accounts have deviated from the approved CloudFormation templates for critical infrastructure. Which CloudFormation feature can help detect these deviations?',
  'mcq',
  '["CloudFormation StackSets","CloudFormation drift detection","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Config conformance packs"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (CloudFormation drift detection) is the correct choice. CloudFormation drift detection allows you to identify when the actual configuration of stack resources differs from their expected configuration in the CloudFormation template. This is crucial for identifying security gaps introduced by manual changes outside of the approved infrastructure-as-code process. Option A (CloudFormation StackSets) is for deploying stacks across multiple accounts/Regions. Option C (AWS Service Catalog) is for provisioning approved IT services. Option D (AWS Config conformance packs) are for continuous compliance assessment against rules, not specifically for detecting deviations from CloudFormation templates.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain59_12',
  NOW(),
  109,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_59_4',
  'medium'
);

